### WolfCafe ###
# src/main/resources/application.properties is deliberately NOT ignored.
#
# It used to hold plaintext secrets, which is why it was excluded. It now
# contains only ${ENV_VAR:default} placeholders -- every real value (database
# password, JWT secret, seeded account password) is supplied through the
# environment at run time. The file has to be in version control because the
# Docker image is built from a clean checkout and the app will not start
# without it.
#
# The test copy stays ignored; see src/test/resources/.gitignore and the
# application.properties.template beside it.
